## Quick Reference Commands

```bash
# Full pre-commit (backend + web + integration + e2e)
./scripts/pre-commit.sh

# Manual equivalent
cd backend && \
  ./gradlew spotlessApply --no-daemon && \
  ./gradlew compileJava compileTestJava --no-daemon && \
  ./gradlew test --no-daemon && \
  ./gradlew integrationTest --no-daemon && \
  cd ../web && npm ci && npm run lint && npm run test && \
  npx playwright install chromium && npm run test:e2e && npm run build && \
  echo "✅ All checks passed - safe to commit"
```

## When to Skip (NEVER for production code)

The ONLY acceptable reasons to skip steps:

| Change type | Skip |
|-------------|------|
| Documentation only (`docs/**`, `*.md`) | Steps 1–5; still do 7–10 |
| Backend only, no web | Step 5 (web) |
| Web only, no backend | Steps 1–4 (backend) |
| Config / formatting only | Step 3–4 if no Java logic changed; still run Step 1 |

Do **not** skip web or backend tests on cross-cutting or security changes.

## Common Issues and Fixes

### Spotless Fails
```bash
cd backend && ./gradlew spotlessApply --no-daemon  # Auto-fix
```

### Backend Tests Fail
- Read the failure message
- Fix the code or test
- Re-run tests
- Do NOT bypass with `@Disabled`

### Integration Tests Fail
- Ensure Docker is running
- Re-run: `cd backend && ./gradlew integrationTest --no-daemon`

### Web: `npm ci` Fails
- Use Node.js 22 (same as CI)
- Delete `web/node_modules` and re-run `npm ci`

### Playwright E2E Fails Locally
- Install browser: `cd web && npx playwright install chromium`
- If port 5173 is in use, stop other dev servers or let Playwright reuse (see `web/README.md`)

### Compilation Errors
- Fix all errors before proceeding
- Do NOT commit code that doesn't compile

---

**REMEMBER**: A broken commit wastes everyone's time. Take a few minutes to verify
rather than hours debugging a broken build.
